<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Medical image fusion</h3>

<figure id="S5.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.09427v1/06.png" id="S5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/238;" width="476" height="238" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Fusion and super-resolution (scale:8) results for FS-Diff as well as the fusion results for the compared methods on the Harvard medical image dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The results of the subjective and objective assessments of the MIF task, under the condition where both image modalities are blurred, are presented in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 Medical image fusion ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FS-Diff: Semantic Guidance and Clarity-Aware Simultaneous Multimodal Image Fusion and Super-Resolution" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Figure <a href="#S5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 5.3 Medical image fusion ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FS-Diff: Semantic Guidance and Clarity-Aware Simultaneous Multimodal Image Fusion and Super-Resolution" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. In Figure <a href="#S5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 5.3 Medical image fusion ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FS-Diff: Semantic Guidance and Clarity-Aware Simultaneous Multimodal Image Fusion and Super-Resolution" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, the comparison methods are fuzzy or even lost when processing structure and color information. For example, BDLFusion, U2Fusion, and DDPM fail to effectively retain marginal skeletal information on MRI, whereas CDD exhibits poor retention of color information and distortion on PET/SPECT images. The third column in Figure <a href="#S5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 5.3 Medical image fusion ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FS-Diff: Semantic Guidance and Clarity-Aware Simultaneous Multimodal Image Fusion and Super-Resolution" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the results of FS-Diff at <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\times 8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" lspace="0.222em" mathvariant="bold" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>𝟖</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\times 8}</annotation></semantics></math> magnification (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>16</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>128</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>). The fusion results generated by FS-Diff retained excellent edges, contrasts, and structures.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 Medical image fusion ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FS-Diff: Semantic Guidance and Clarity-Aware Simultaneous Multimodal Image Fusion and Super-Resolution" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, our FS-Diff consistently performed well in terms of the VIF, Q<sup id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">AB/F</sup>, SSIM, PSNR, and LPIPS metrics on the MRI-PET and MRI-SPECT MIF datasets slightly lagged behind U2Fusion<span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">in terms of the MSE. Notably,</span> although the results of the comparison method were obtained via multimodal HR source image fusion and then down-sampling (<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256^{2}\rightarrow 128^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>256</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>128</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256^{2}\rightarrow 128^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), the subjective and objective assessments were still inferior to the results of FS-Diff (<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16^{2}\rightarrow 128^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>16</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>128</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16^{2}\rightarrow 128^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), which fully proved the effectiveness of FS-Diff on MIF.</p>
</div>
